{
  "_comment": "Curated control panels, keyed by romset shortname. These OVERRIDE analog-controls.json, which is generated from driver source. Driver source records which input ports a board reads; it does not record what the player's hands were on, and inferring one from the other produced a string of wrong panels: a rotary joystick split into a stick and a knob, cabinets given pedals they never had, Atari's rotary games missed entirely because their drivers lack the comment Data East's carry. Anything in this file is a statement about a real machine and can be corrected by anyone who has seen one. Keep it to games people actually play; the generated data still covers the long tail.",

